Scope clarification from the Phase A provenance audit:
The nazuchem repository's crates/nazuchem-s2n/src/ began as a port of
openclatura 0.4.3, extended in ReShiki. The introductory source description
above records that lineage; the current JSON registries include both copied
and locally adapted data, and source modules also contain separately
identified local implementations. The nazuchem repository-root
PROVENANCE-nazuchem.toml and Rust source/function headers record those
boundaries, upstream paths and pins. OPSIN-derived data retains its own
source/version statements; not every underlying generation revision is known.

The nazuchem repository's crates/nazuchem-s2n/src/python_int_set.rs adapts
CPython 3.12 Objects/setobject.c under Python-2.0. Its exact patch/commit is
unresolved; see licenses/cpython/LICENSE and licenses/cpython/NOTICE for the
complete licence/history and the source-pin qualification. It is not asserted
to be original code or covered solely by openclatura's MIT grant.

The retained IUPAC table data/bluebook/p25_retained.tsv remains NOASSERTION
pending the owner's reuse-permission decision. The PubChem-derived
tests/fixtures/s2n/bakeoff_corpus.tsv is test-only, excluded from packages,
and remains NOASSERTION pending the owner's source-terms decision. The MIT
statement above does not grant rights to these unresolved materials.
